details:
It was discovered that the io_uring subsystem in the Linux kernel contained
a memory leak when handling certain asynchronous commands. A local attacker
could possibly use this to cause a denial of service (memory exhaustion).
(CVE-2026-80811)

It was discovered that the io_uring subsystem in the Linux kernel did not
properly validate the size of certain query requests. A local attacker
could possibly use this to cause a denial of service (system hang).
(CVE-2026-81009)

It was discovered that the io_uring subsystem in the Linux kernel did not
properly handle canceled task work when processing certain wait operations,
leading to the operation being performed in the wrong task context. A local
attacker could possibly use this to cause a denial of service (system
crash). (CVE-2026-81010)

It was discovered that the io_uring subsystem in the Linux kernel did not
properly track buffer consumption when receiving truncated network
messages. A remote attacker could possibly use this to corrupt the receive
buffers of certain applications, resulting in a denial of service or
another unspecified impact. (CVE-2026-97618)

Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.
An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.
